A brief note: conditions 1 and 2 are ordinary, well-established license
terms and hold up the way any open-source license does. Condition 3 is
less conventional — it's a clear, good-faith expectation rather than a
clause with a defined percentage or trigger, so treat it as a strong
statement of intent rather than a fully self-enforcing contract term.

